The `WordPair` and `ChallengeType` field docs scope the migration semantics to FCW, but the computation that reads them covers apostrophe usage and subject-verb agreement as well. The added field comments say:

```go
// ChallengeType is the type of challenge this attempt targeted, stored
// on the attempt so the FCW proven-pair computation can be type-scoped
...
// WordPair is the canonicalized confused-word pair of the challenge
// this attempt targeted, stored for the same reason. Empty means
// "needs migration" only for FCW attempts — a challenge with no
// IncorrectForm token legitimately yields "".
```

The consumer, `_computeCorrectPairs` in `services/ai-guide/langlit/handlers.go`, is parameterized by `challengeType` and is called for frequently-confused-words, apostrophe usage, and subject-verb agreement alike (see `wordPairType` in `langlit_challenge_component.go`), and its cold-attempt branch treats an empty `WordPair` as needing migration regardless of type. Dropping "FCW" from both sentences — "so the proven-pair computation can be type-scoped", "Empty means 'needs migration' for any word-pair type" — matches what the code does.
